    "q-95428": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95428",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=6\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(\\frac{x}{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+1}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
