    "q-341820": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341820",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $24{x}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4})}^{′} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{9}{x}^{8}+1}}\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3} \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{\\frac{4{x}^{8}+9}{9}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{8}+9}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
