    "q-341798": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341798",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=5\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(3x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(3x)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(3x)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(3x)^{2}+1}}\\cdot (3x)^{′} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}+1}}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
