    "q-95500": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95500",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{ln}^{2}⁡x-1}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{ln}^{2}⁡x-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
