    "q-344313": {
      "dom_id": "step-q344313",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=4\\,\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(4x-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(4x-1)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(4x-1)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-(4x-1)^{2}}\\cdot (4x-1)^{′} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-(16{x}^{2}-8x+1)}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{1}{8x-16{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{1}{8x(1-2x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x(1-2x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
