    "q-337914": {
      "dom_id": "step-q337914",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\,\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(2x-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(2x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(2x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(2x-1)}^{2}}\\cdot {(2x-1)}^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-(4{x}^{2}-4x+1)}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4x-4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4x(1-x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x(1-x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
