    "q-95512": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95512",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{3}),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{3})}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{3})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{(1-\\frac{{x}^{12}}{9})}\\cdot 2{x}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{9{x}^{5}}{9-{x}^{12}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
